{
  "id": "sixth-floor",
  "name": "The Sixth Floor",
  "description": "A squatted flat on the sixth floor of the condemned tower in the dead blocks, made into a home by people who live off the grid. Bare concrete and strips of old wallpaper, a hole in the ceiling's corner open to the sky. A big window sheeted in plastic and half boarded, the paying block's warm windows and the Ribbon's lights beyond. A door laid on cinder blocks for a table with an oil lamp, cushions and an armchair; a camping stove, a water barrel and plank shelves of jars and herbs under battery fairy lights; a mattress on pallets under patchwork quilts beside crates crammed with paper, letters and ledgers tied with string, candles in jars, and a hand-drawn map of the neighbourhood. A curtain over the doorway to the dark stairwell, a lantern on a nail beside it.",
